0015: def main(input_grid):
0016:     """
0017:     Punch alternating black holes through the center line of each monochromatic 3-wide rectangle.
0018: 
0019:     Input structure:
0020:     - The grid contains one or more separated non-black monochromatic rectangles.
0021:     - Each rectangle has short side length 3 and an odd long side.
0022:     - Rectangles may be horizontal or vertical on a black background.
0023: 
0024:     Rule:
0025:     - Detect each rectangle and rotate vertical ones into a horizontal working orientation.
0026:     - Set every other pixel along the middle line, starting one pixel in, to black.
0027:     - Restore the original orientation and paste the edited rectangle back onto a black output.
0028: 
0029:     Key insight:
0030:     - The hole pattern is defined along the rectangle's long axis, so orientation is handled
0031:       by canonicalizing the rectangle before editing it.
0032:     """
0033:     # Plan:
0034:     # 1. Extract the rectangles from the input grid
0035:     # 2. Canonicalize the rectangles: ensure that they are horizontal (remember to rotate back otherwise)
0036:     # 3. Draw black pixels inside each rectangle (horizontally, skipping every other pixel)
0037:     # 4. Rotate the rectangle back if it was not originally horizontal
0038: 
